\b Restart Using Disk
\b0 \
\
This script is like the Restart Choosing Disk script, but it requires no user interaction. Instead, it immediately restarts the computer using a hard-coded disk name. Edit the disk name property in the script before running this example script.\
\

\b Safari - Search Google
\b0 \
\
This script demonstrates how to fill in a text field on a Web site. Using a 'set value' command to set the value of the text field works correctly on Mac OS X 10.6.0 and newer. (On earlier system versions, 'set value' does not "stick". Instead, assign keyboard focus to the text field and then send the text to the target application using the 'keystroke' command.)}